{title: 466 - Wonderful Peace}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #466 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 466}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Far away in the depths of my [C]spirit to[G]night,
Rolls a melody [A7]sweeter than [D]psalm;
In [G]celestial like strains it un[C]ceasingly falls
O’er my [G]soul like an [D7]infinite [G]calm.
Peace! Peace! [C]wonderful [G]peace,
Coming [Em]down from the [A7]Father [D]above;
Sweep [G]over my spirit for[C]ever, I pray,
In [G]fathomless [D7]billows of [G]love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]Peace! [C]Peace! [G]wonderful peace,
[A7]Coming down from [D]the Father above;
[G]Sweep over my [C]spirit forever, I pray,
[G]In [D7]fathomless billows [G]of love.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]What a treasure [C]I have in [G]this wonderful peace,
[A7]Buried deep in [D]my inner most soul,
[G]So secure that no [C]power can mine it away,
[G]While the [D7]years of [G]eternity roll!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I believe when [C]I rise to [G]that city of peace,
[A7]Where the Author of [D]peace I shall see,
[G]That one strain of the [C]song which the ransomed will sing,
[G]In that [D7]heavenly kingdom [G]will be-
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Weary soul, [C]without gladness or [G]comfort or rest,
[A7]Passing down the [D]rough pathway of time!
[G]Make the Savior your friend [C]ere the shadows grow dark;
[G]O accept [D7]of this [G]peace so sublime.
{end_of_verse}
